50 730 Td (PHOTOSYNTHESIS: ENERGY FROM SUNLIGHT) Tj
50 712 Td () Tj
50 694 Td (Photosynthesis is the process by which plants, algae, and some bacteria convert light energy) Tj
50 676 Td (into chemical energy stored in sugar molecules. It occurs primarily in the chloroplasts of) Tj
50 658 Td (plant cells.) Tj
50 640 Td () Tj
50 622 Td (The overall balanced equation for photosynthesis is: 6 CO2 + 6 H2O + light energy -> C6H12O6 +) Tj
50 604 Td (6 O2. Carbon dioxide and water are consumed, and glucose and oxygen gas are produced.) Tj
50 586 Td () Tj
50 568 Td (Photosynthesis happens in two major stages: the light-dependent reactions and the) Tj
50 550 Td (light-independent reactions, also known as the Calvin cycle. The light-dependent reactions) Tj
50 532 Td (capture energy from sunlight and produce ATP and NADPH. The Calvin cycle uses ATP and NADPH to) Tj
50 514 Td (convert carbon dioxide into glucose.) Tj
50 496 Td () Tj
50 478 Td (CHLOROPLAST STRUCTURE) Tj
50 460 Td () Tj
50 442 Td (Chloroplasts are double-membrane organelles. Inside is the stroma, a fluid-filled space, and) Tj
50 424 Td (the thylakoids, flattened membrane sacs stacked into structures called grana. Chlorophyll, the) Tj
50 406 Td (pigment that gives plants their green color, is embedded in the thylakoid membranes and) Tj
50 388 Td (absorbs light most strongly in the blue-violet and red regions of the spectrum.) Tj
ET
