50 730 Td (LIGHT-DEPENDENT REACTIONS) Tj
50 712 Td () Tj
50 694 Td (The light-dependent reactions take place in the thylakoid membranes. When a photon of light) Tj
50 676 Td (strikes a chlorophyll molecule, an electron is excited to a higher energy level. This electron) Tj
50 658 Td (is passed along an electron transport chain, releasing energy that pumps protons into the) Tj
50 640 Td (thylakoid lumen.) Tj
50 622 Td () Tj
50 604 Td (The buildup of protons creates an electrochemical gradient. ATP synthase, an enzyme embedded) Tj
50 586 Td (in the thylakoid membrane, uses this gradient to produce ATP in a process called) Tj
50 568 Td (photophosphorylation. Water molecules are split to replace the lost electrons, releasing) Tj
50 550 Td (oxygen gas as a byproduct. The electrons ultimately reduce NADP+ to form NADPH.) Tj
50 532 Td () Tj
50 514 Td (Key particles of the light-dependent reactions: Photosystem II absorbs light and initiates the) Tj
50 496 Td (electron transport chain; Photosystem I re-energizes the electrons and passes them to NADP+) Tj
50 478 Td (reductase to form NADPH. The movement of protons through ATP synthase produces about three ATP) Tj
50 460 Td (molecules per gradient cycle.) Tj
ET
endstream
