50 730 Td (THE CALVIN CYCLE) Tj
50 712 Td () Tj
50 694 Td (The Calvin cycle, also called the light-independent reactions or the dark reactions, occurs in) Tj
50 676 Td (the stroma of the chloroplast. It does not require light directly, but it depends on the ATP) Tj
50 658 Td (and NADPH produced by the light-dependent reactions.) Tj
50 640 Td () Tj
50 622 Td (The Calvin cycle has three phases: carbon fixation, reduction, and regeneration.) Tj
50 604 Td () Tj
50 586 Td (In carbon fixation, the enzyme rubisco attaches carbon dioxide to ribulose biphosphate, or) Tj
50 568 Td (RuBP, a five-carbon molecule. This produces an unstable six-carbon compound that immediately) Tj
50 550 Td (splits into two molecules of 3-phosphoglycerate \(3-PGA\).) Tj
50 532 Td () Tj
50 514 Td (During reduction, ATP and NADPH supply energy and electrons to convert 3-PGA into) Tj
50 496 Td (glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate \(G3P\). One out of every six G3P molecules exits the cycle to form) Tj
50 478 Td (glucose and other carbohydrates.) Tj
50 460 Td () Tj
50 442 Td (In the regeneration phase, the remaining G3P molecules are rearranged and, with the help of) Tj
50 424 Td (ATP, rebuilt into RuBP so the cycle can continue.) Tj
ET
endstream
