50 730 Td (FACTORS AFFECTING PHOTOSYNTHESIS RATE) Tj
50 712 Td () Tj
50 694 Td (Several environmental factors limit the rate of photosynthesis. Light intensity increases the) Tj
50 676 Td (rate up to a saturation point beyond which additional light has no effect. Carbon dioxide) Tj
50 658 Td (concentration similarly raises the rate until other factors become limiting. Temperature) Tj
50 640 Td (affects the enzymes involved; photosynthesis slows at very high temperatures because enzymes) Tj
50 622 Td (denature.) Tj
50 604 Td () Tj
50 586 Td (The concept of the limiting factor states that the rate of a process is limited by the factor) Tj
50 568 Td (present at its lowest amount. For example, at night or in very dim light, light is the) Tj
50 550 Td (limiting factor; on a bright day in a sealed glasshouse, carbon dioxide may become the) Tj
50 532 Td (limiting factor.) Tj
50 514 Td () Tj
50 496 Td (Photorespiration is a wasteful process in which rubisco reacts with oxygen instead of carbon) Tj
50 478 Td (dioxide, producing a two-carbon compound that must be broken down, wasting energy. Some) Tj
50 460 Td (plants, called C4 plants, avoid photorespiration by spatially separating carbon fixation and) Tj
50 442 Td (the Calvin cycle.) Tj
ET
endstream
