50 730 Td (SUMMARY OF PHOTOSYNTHESIS) Tj
50 712 Td () Tj
50 694 Td (Photosynthesis converts light energy into chemical energy stored in glucose. It requires) Tj
50 676 Td (carbon dioxide and water and releases oxygen. The process is powered by the light-dependent) Tj
50 658 Td (reactions, which produce ATP and NADPH, and the Calvin cycle, which uses these molecules to) Tj
50 640 Td (fix carbon dioxide into sugar.) Tj
50 622 Td () Tj
50 604 Td (The main structures involved are the thylakoid membranes, where light absorption and the) Tj
50 586 Td (electron transport chain occur, and the stroma, where the Calvin cycle happens. The key) Tj
50 568 Td (enzymes are ATP synthase, rubisco, and NADP+ reductase.) Tj
50 550 Td () Tj
50 532 Td (Rate of photosynthesis is influenced by light intensity, carbon dioxide concentration, and) Tj
50 514 Td (temperature. Plants have evolved adaptations like C4 and CAM pathways to limit) Tj
50 496 Td (photorespiration and survive harsh environments.) Tj
ET
endstream
